[h1]Ship Core Framework[/h1]

Ship Core Framework is a modular, multiplayer-focused alternative to Keen's block-limit system, inspired by [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3193738565]Ship Classes[/url] and rebuilt from the ground up.

Physical Ship Core blocks define what a grid may build and how it performs. Profiles can control block limits, size, mass, PCU, speed, friction, production, power, defense, abilities, ownership, upgrades, and connector behavior.

[b]This is a framework, not a core pack.[/b] Use a dependent core mod, create your own configuration, or configure the No Core profile.

[h2]Features[/h2]

[list]
[*]Deterministic main and backup cores across mechanical grid groups
[*]Block, mass, PCU, minimum-size, player, faction, and manifest limits
[*]Reusable block groups, exclusions, weights, and directional rules
[*]Shutoff, damage, delete/refund, and explosion punishments
[*]Thruster, gyro, refinery, assembler, drill, and power modifiers
[*]Speed limits, boosts, friction curves, cruise behavior, and atmospheric friction
[*]Passive/active defense and power-overclock abilities
[*]Upgrade modules with stat, capacity, and block-limit modifiers
[*]Faction-rank requirements and ownership validation
[*]Connector blacklists and connected-grid punishment rules
[*]No-fly zones and optional Nexus multi-sector synchronization
[*]Server-authoritative, cached, event-driven enforcement
[/list]

[h2]Player Tools[/h2]

[list]
[*]Live build preview for limits, mass, PCU, and projected capacity
[*]Direction arrows, invalid-placement boxes, and first-core axes
[*]Backup-core guidance; backups must match the main core orientation
[*]Live Core HUD for piloted or aimed friendly grids; toggle with [b]Numpad 0[/b] or [b]/corehud[/b]
[*]Persistent Core HUD keybind and enabled state; configure the key in the Text HUD API player menu
[*]Core Status LCD dashboards with limits, modifiers, and punishment reasons
[*][b]/core info[/b], [b]/core limits[/b], and grace countdowns
[/list]

[h2]Example Core Pack[/h2]

[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3552605473]Arcane Cores[/url] demonstrates combat, fighter, utility, and station profiles with specialized limits, modifiers, abilities, upgrades, and docking rules.

[h2]Mod API v4[/h2]

SCF includes separate role-specific APIs:

[list]
[*][b]ShipCoreFrameworkServerApi[/b] for authoritative server access
[*][b]ShipCoreFrameworkClientApi[/b] for synchronized read-only client data
[*]Configuration, runtime, readiness, core, grid, limit, modifier, speed, ability, ownership, and event data
[/list]

[b]API v4 is a breaking upgrade.[/b] API v3 integrations must migrate.

[h2]Configurator and Documentation[/h2]

The configurator creates, imports, validates, and exports complete SCF configurations. It can also open an existing mod/Data folder and update generated XML files in place.

[url=https://owendb1.github.io/arcane-systems/scf-configurator/]Open the XML Configurator[/url]

The framework documentation contains the current XML reference, commands, examples, upgrade stats, API instructions, and runtime behavior:

[url=https://github.com/OwendB1/arcane-systems/blob/main/docs/ship-core-framework.md]Read the Ship Core Framework Documentation[/url]

[h2]Common Questions[/h2]

[b]How do I select a class?[/b]
Build a physical core supplied by a dependent mod. Grids without one use the configured No Core profile.

[b]How do I see limits?[/b]
Use the build-preview HUD, Core Status LCD, [b]/core info[/b], or [b]/core limits[/b].

[b]Does it support servers and subgrids?[/b]
Yes. SCF is server-authoritative and tracks mechanical grid groups, including rotors, hinges, and pistons. Connector behavior is configurable.

[b]Can this replace a block limiter?[/b]
Yes. Limits can apply per grid group, core, player, faction, and manifest.

[b]Are minimum limits supported?[/b]
Yes, with a configurable grace countdown.

[b]Can I make a core pack?[/b]
Yes. Start with the configurator, framework documentation, and Arcane Cores example.

